invariant: INV-26
file: aes_hw.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh aes-equiv
reason: the x86-64 AES-256 key expansion stops after round key 13 and never
  stores round key 14, so the last round of every TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384
  block runs under whatever the caller's schedule held. bin/aes_equiv_test
  expands into a buffer it did not clear and compares all fifteen round
  keys with the table's byte for byte. Only an x86-64 compiler reads the
  lines, so the script builds that binary for x86-64 and runs it under
  qemu-x86_64.

--- old
    first = next_round_key(first, second, round_constant);
    store_block(&round_keys[(AES_256_ROUND_KEYS - 1) * AES_BLOCK], first);
--- new
